NAME "Draw: Ollama prompt concatenation"

-- This template is a walkthrough for the draw screen.
-- Open it in game with:
-- /sfm draw template open draw_ollama_prompt_concatenation

-- Goal:
-- Build a slash command text element whose final text is:
-- /sfm draw ollama run llama3.2 "Summarize the contents of lane A in one sentence."

-- Minimal construction from an empty canvas:
-- 1. Create a text element for the prefix:
--    /sfm draw ollama run llama3.2 "Summarize 
-- 2. Create a second text element immediately to the right for the parameter:
--    the contents of lane A
-- 3. Create a third text element immediately to the right for the suffix:
--     in one sentence."
-- 4. Draw one rectangle that covers all three text elements.
--    Example:
--    /box 32 32 620 52
-- 5. Add a slash command text element anywhere:
--    /concatenate @rect[40,40]
-- 6. Running that command emits a new text element containing the full
--    /sfm draw ollama run ... command.
-- 7. Edit only the middle text element to change the parameter, then rerun
--    /concatenate.

-- Why this works:
-- - concatenate captures glyphs whose bounds overlap the selected rectangle(s)
-- - captured glyphs are ordered by Y first and X second
-- - text on the same line becomes a single-line prompt
-- - text on different lines produces newline-separated prompt text

-- Shared-anchor variant:
-- If you want true union-of-rectangles composition instead of one big box,
-- make every participating box contain the same selector point.
-- Example selector point: 8,8
-- Then all participating boxes can be addressed with:
-- /concatenate @rect[8,8]
-- Keep unrelated text away from that shared anchor corridor, otherwise its
-- glyphs can be captured too.

-- Suggested shared-anchor boxes for prefix, parameter, and suffix on one line:
-- /box 0 0 260 28
-- /box 0 0 430 28
-- /box 0 0 620 28

-- Final step:
-- Once the emitted text looks right, run the emitted
-- /sfm draw ollama run ... slash command text element.

EVERY 20 TICKS DO
    -- placeholder body so the template card renders without parser errors
    INPUT FROM a
    OUTPUT TO b
END